Depends: ${misc:Depends}, vanilla-gnome-desktop, gnome-session, gnome-software, gnome-software-plugin-flatpak, flatpak, adwaita-icon-theme, gnome-themes-extra, ubuntu-wallpapers, zsh, zsh-common, git, ca-certificates, zsh-autosuggestions, zsh-syntax-highlighting
Conflicts: snapd, snapd-desktop-integration, gnome-software-plugin-snap, gnome-shell-extension-ubuntu-dock, yaru-theme-gnome-shell, yaru-theme-gtk, yaru-theme-icon, yaru-theme-sound, yaru-theme-unity
Breaks: snapd, snapd-desktop-integration, gnome-software-plugin-snap, gnome-shell-extension-ubuntu-dock, yaru-theme-gnome-shell, yaru-theme-gtk, yaru-theme-icon, yaru-theme-sound, yaru-theme-unity
Description: TinhMenhDo Ubuntu vanilla GNOME and Flatpak metapackage
 TinhMenhDo Ubuntu configures an Ubuntu desktop around the vanilla GNOME
 desktop packages, GNOME Software and Flatpak. It conflicts with Snap, the
 Ubuntu Dock extension and Yaru theme packages so APT cannot keep them
 installed alongside this profile. Adwaita is installed as the neutral GNOME
 theme/icon fallback. The Ubuntu wallpaper package remains required by
 Ubuntu's GNOME Shell package on supported releases and is not a Yaru theme.
 .
 This package deliberately does not purge user data, call apt recursively,
 add third-party repositories, or install a browser from a PPA. It provides
 a Zsh setup with Oh My Zsh, common plugins, and persistent history.
